meta {
  name: List persons
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons?limit=50
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.school: eq {{schoolCode}}
  res.body.persons: isArray
  res.body.count: gte 3
}

docs {
  Reads back the three people created above.

  count is how many rows this caller may see, not how many rows exist. The
  query is narrowed to the viewer before it is counted, so the same request
  run with a class teacher's token returns a smaller count than an
  administrator's, and neither is wrong.

  Filters: q (name, email, phone), status, cas_user_id. Paging: limit, offset.
  An unrecognised filter value is ignored rather than rejected, so do not read
  a 200 here as proof that your filter was understood.
}
